# GetEUICCChallenge (ES10b, SGP.22 v2.6 section 5.7.7), hand-built.
#
# The challenge is sixteen bytes the eUICC picks at random, so a capture
# of a real one would pin nothing about this code -- any sixteen bytes
# would do. These are 00..0F, chosen to be recognisable, which is also
# what lets the test assert the exact value rather than only the length:
# a decoder that returned the right count of the wrong bytes would pass
# a length check and fail this.
#
# The SELECT ISD-R exchange is this project's own test card's real FCI.
